# The UI layout gate's fixtures are a CAPTURE, not source.
#
# `tests/ui-layout-gate/README.md` records a sha256 for each captured file so a
# reader can prove the copy here is the CEO's 31 Aug 2026 capture byte for byte.
# On Windows checkouts git would otherwise rewrite LF to CRLF and every one of
# those hashes would be wrong on someone else's machine — a provenance claim
# that fails for a reason that has nothing to do with provenance.
tests/ui-layout-gate/fixtures/** -text

# UI-13. Same reasoning as `scripts/git-hooks/.gitattributes` (RISK-09), which
# only covers its own directory: this repo has core.autocrlf=true on Windows and
# no repo-wide rule, so a shell script committed here checks out with CRLF. The
# UI layout gate runs `scripts/measure/check-h6.sh` on ubuntu-latest, where a
# shebang ending in CR fails with "bad interpreter" — a blocking gate that is
# present, executable and cannot run.
scripts/**/*.sh text eol=lf
